      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Sathorn Unique Tower, halted in 1997, remains a derelict 47‑storey ghost tower, attracting urban explorers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sathorn_Unique_Tower",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Sathorn Mansion, former home of Luang Sathon, still stands in the middle of Sathorn Road, a relic of the area's past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://propertysights.com/articles/sathorn-bangkok-thailand/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sathorn preserves Thai charm with hidden shrines, wet markets, and the Sri Maha Mariamman Hindu Temple’s vivid colors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://go2bkk.com/bangkok-sathorn/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wat Yannawa, a boat‑shaped temple on the Chao Phraya’s edge, sits opposite the Sathorn area and reflects the district’s river heritage.",
